      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.67,
      "end_seconds": 5.96,
      "duration_seconds": 5.29,
      "text": "I mean, good evening, doctor, thanks for seeing me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.89,
      "end_seconds": 10.99,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "yes, have a a seat tell me what's going on"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 13.05,
      "end_seconds": 20.0,
      "duration_seconds": 6.95,
      "text": "So the thing is I've got a tremor in my right hand at rest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.96,
      "end_seconds": 23.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "So, did it come on recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.94,
      "end_seconds": 35.67,
      "duration_seconds": 10.73,
      "text": "it's been like this since yesterday. I'm not great at remembering details you know so bear with me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.64,
      "end_seconds": 41.81,
      "duration_seconds": 5.17,
      "text": "Okay give me more detail on it whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.37,
      "end_seconds": 49.69,
      "duration_seconds": 6.32,
      "text": "uh, I'd say severe. I get some relief from using the hand"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 53.88,
      "end_seconds": 56.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "does anything else come with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.12,
      "end_seconds": 80.08,
      "duration_seconds": 22.96,
      "text": "yeah, uh, when it starts I tend to get smaller handwriting as well okay, so as for smaller handwriting, I honestly can't say when that began it might have been last month or the month before"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 80.36,
      "end_seconds": 81.3,
      "duration_seconds": 0.94,
      "text": "hm okay"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.84,
      "end_seconds": 91.67,
      "duration_seconds": 8.83,
      "text": "I've I've also had a stiff arm for about a month. About stiff arm I'd say mild."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.24,
      "end_seconds": 94.49,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.21,
      "end_seconds": 98.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "No, I've never smoked in my life"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.8,
      "end_seconds": 104.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "do you drink alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.49,
      "end_seconds": 108.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "I only drink at family occasions"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.45,
      "end_seconds": 111.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Tell me about your eating."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.59,
      "end_seconds": 119.67,
      "duration_seconds": 6.08,
      "text": "I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.68,
      "end_seconds": 122.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "and your job?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.04,
      "end_seconds": 127.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.55,
      "text": "I work in accounts at a hospital"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.58,
      "end_seconds": 130.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "Do you live by yourself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.45,
      "end_seconds": 136.45,
      "duration_seconds": 5.0,
      "text": "No, I share a house with my brother"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.5,
      "end_seconds": 143.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "Do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.23,
      "end_seconds": 147.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "it's metformin, twice a day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.31,
      "end_seconds": 151.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "do you know the dose?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.74,
      "end_seconds": 157.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.63,
      "text": "500 milligrams I think that's what's on the box"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.97,
      "end_seconds": 173.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.74,
      "end_seconds": 177.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "I've I've had diabetes yes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.71,
      "end_seconds": 190.71,
      "duration_seconds": 11.0,
      "text": "I see go ahead okay I can see diabetes in your file as well are there any allergies I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 192.19,
      "end_seconds": 198.17,
      "duration_seconds": 5.98,
      "text": "I'm allergic to plasters, I get a red itchy rash"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.48,
      "end_seconds": 205.45,
      "duration_seconds": 5.97,
      "text": "Have you had any falls, constipation, memory problems or loss of smell?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 210.96,
      "end_seconds": 214.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "no, you know, I'd have said so"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.27,
      "end_seconds": 219.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "how about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 221.18,
      "end_seconds": 222.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "Nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.48,
      "end_seconds": 226.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "and your skin, any changes there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 227.68,
      "end_seconds": 230.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "so no skin's been fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.31,
      "end_seconds": 234.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "shall I start the examination?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.67,
      "end_seconds": 237.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "Fine by me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.6,
      "end_seconds": 240.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "so, does that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.98,
      "end_seconds": 261.3,
      "duration_seconds": 9.32,
      "text": "there is a pill-rolling tremor at rest on the right and the arm is stiff with a cogwheel feel"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.41,
      "end_seconds": 266.26,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "Please sit back down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.46,
      "end_seconds": 291.59,
      "duration_seconds": 10.13,
      "text": "Okay so so my impression is this: I think we're dealing with possible Parkinson's disease at this stage. I can't rule out a drug-induced tremor yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 293.1,
      "end_seconds": 296.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "I'm scared it's something bad. Is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.11,
      "end_seconds": 304.95,
      "duration_seconds": 6.84,
      "text": "I can't promise yet but most people with possible Parkinson's disease do well once it's treated properly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.76,
      "end_seconds": 339.23,
      "duration_seconds": 25.47,
      "text": "I want a blood test done, that's for tremor. I'm referring you to the specialist and meanwhile keep active. Try to keep a simple diary of when it happens and what you were doing, and bring it to the next visit. The thing that would worry me is if the symptoms get worse. If that happens, go to emergency"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 340.15,
      "end_seconds": 342.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "Alright, you know, I follow."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 343.95,
      "end_seconds": 346.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 348.45,
      "end_seconds": 352.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "ah, great, thank you for your help"
    }
  ]
